From 21c1607fe52875b66afc1616f45c8a14a0b97471 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x4pro-emu <x4pro-emu@localhost>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 19:11:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] xteink-x4pro: analog-master I2C block, SENS/SAR ADC,
 radio register stub, capped access loggers

The stock xteink_app's WiFi start parked its radio task (priority 23, core 0)
in polls that the SoC's silent catch-all never satisfied, starving the UI:
ROM rom_pkdet_vol_start on the analog-master block (0x6000E050 bits 26:24),
then the PHY on SENS TSENS_READY (0x60008850 bit 8), FE 0x60006174 bit 16
(capture done) and WiFi MAC 0x60033D14 bit 0 (ready). None has a timeout.

- hw/misc/x4pro_ana_i2c.c: I2C_ANA_MST at 0x6000E000. Command words of the
  two regi2c masters (block | reg<<8 | data<<16, write bit 24, busy bit 25,
  start bit 26; protocol from the ROM), analog registers stored per (block,
  register), ANA_CONF0 with CAL_DONE, SAR2 power-detector control idle/done
  and eight samples from the "sar2-code" property.
- hw/misc/esp32s3_saradc.c: SENS at 0x60008800. MEAS1/MEAS2 oneshots complete
  on the next read (DONE + "sar1-data"/"sar2-data"), the temperature sensor
  is always ready ("tsens-out"), everything else reads back as written.
- hw/misc/esp32s3_rfstub.c: FE2/FE/RX/BB/WiFi-MAC storage stub with status
  bits that read as set (FE +0x174.16, MAC +0xD14.0); the "sticky" property
  adds "0xADDR:0xMASK" entries at run time.
- include/hw/misc/x4pro_hotlog.h: the I/O access loggers and the stub log the
  first 32 accesses per address and count the rest; the board state JSON lists
  the addresses polled past the cap ("iolog_hot", "rf.hot"). One PHY poll had
  written 1.9 GB of qemu.log in 30 s before.
- xteink_x4pro.c: wire the three devices (priority 2), extend the logger table
  to the remaining holes of the map (WDEV around the RNG, BT, SLC, ...), add
  "ana_i2c", "saradc", "rf" and "iolog_hot" to /machine/x4pro-board state.

With the device's NVS (WiFi enabled) the stock now prints "wifi:mode : sta",
"wifi:enable tsf" as on the hardware, then "TX Q not empty" / "force witi
stop" at +7.5 s and deinitialises WiFi at +17.5 s; gauge polls, repaints and
touch continue throughout. No Espressif file is touched.
